# Independent Method Claim

**Claim 1.** A method for forming a metal sheet component, the method comprising:

providing a metal sheet blank between a first die and a second die of a matched die set, the first die and the second die defining a forming cavity corresponding to a desired shape of the metal sheet component;

heating the metal sheet blank to a forming temperature above a Solvus temperature of the metal sheet blank;

initiating a forming stroke by moving at least one of the first die and the second die toward the other to progressively deform the metal sheet blank into conformance with the forming cavity;

pausing the forming stroke at an intermediate position prior to completion of the deformation of the metal sheet blank, thereby defining a dwell period during which further movement of the first die and the second die relative to one another is suspended;

controlling a cooling rate of the metal sheet blank during the dwell period to maintain the metal sheet blank within a predetermined temperature range associated with a target microstructure of the metal sheet component;

resuming the forming stroke after the dwell period to complete the deformation of the metal sheet blank into conformance with the forming cavity, thereby forming the metal sheet component; and

removing the metal sheet component from between the first die and the second die.
